buy_v2_character.user_template:
Compare these two consecutive years of 10-K Item 1A Risk Factors for a {sector} company.

CURRENT YEAR 10-K RISK FACTORS (filed {current_filed}):
{current_risk_factors}

PRIOR YEAR 10-K RISK FACTORS (filed {prior_filed}):
{prior_risk_factors}

Has the fundamental CHARACTER of the company's risk profile changed, or are these the same types of risks as last year? We're not asking if risks got worse — we're asking if the NATURE of what threatens the company has shifted.

Examples of character change: A company that previously faced only competitive risks now faces regulatory/legal risks. A company that had industry-wide risks now has company-specific operational problems.

Respond with JSON only:
{"character_changed": true or false, "assessment": "same_character" or "new_risk_types", "confidence": "high" or "medium" or "low", "new_risk_categories": ["list any fundamentally new types of risk"]}

